# Apps — Workers

Applies to `worker-service`, `worker-aggregation`, and `worker-indexer`.

## `/tasks/*` handlers

Every Cloud Tasks / HTTP task handler must be:

1. **Idempotent** and **retry-safe** (safe on at-least-once delivery)
2. Wrapped with **`withWorkloadRun`** / recorder from `@repo/workload-runs`
3. Registered in `@repo/workload-registry` (see `AGENTS.md` and rule `60-workload-registry`)

Propagate lineage headers when enqueueing further work:

- `X-Workload-Run-Parent-Id`
- `X-Workload-Run-Root-Id`

## AI

- Use `createWorkerAiController` / `runAiRequest` only — never call Vertex clients directly.
- Re-assert spend limits in the worker (authoritative). See `docs/ai-platform/03-cost-guards.md`.
- Surfaces and routes: `docs/ai-platform/05-api-worker-ui.md`.

## Aggregation / indexing

- Follow `docs/guides/aggregations.md` for aggregation workers.
- Inventory: `docs/infrastructure/workload-inventory.md`.

## Do not

- Perform long unbounded Firestore scans without pagination/cursors
- Swallow errors without failing the task when retry is required
- Skip workload run instrumentation “just for local”

## Enforcement

- `pnpm check:workload-coverage`
- Worker package tests / typecheck / lint
- `pnpm check:prod-runtime` when changing deploy bundles

